#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:3
msgid "A CSS selector compiler and engine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:5
msgid "What?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:7
msgid ""
"As a **compiler**, css-select turns CSS selectors into functions that "
"tests if elements match them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:10
msgid ""
"As an **engine**, css-select looks through a DOM tree, searching for "
"elements. Elements are tested \"from the top\", similar to how browsers "
"execute CSS selectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:14
msgid ""
"In its default configuration, css-select queries the DOM structure of the"
" [`domhandler`](https://github.com/fb55/domhandler) module (also known as"
" htmlparser2 DOM). To query alternative DOM structures, see "
"[`Options`](#options) below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:19
msgid "**Features:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:21
msgid "🔬 Full implementation of CSS3 selectors, as well as most CSS4 selectors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:22
msgid ""
"🧪 Partial implementation of jQuery/Sizzle extensions (see [cheerio-"
"select](https://github.com/cheeriojs/cheerio-select) for the remaining "
"selectors)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:25
msgid ""
"🧑‍🔬 High test coverage, including the full test suites from "
"[`Sizzle`](https://github.com/jquery/sizzle), "
"[`Qwery`](https://github.com/ded/qwery) and "
"[`NWMatcher`](https://github.com/dperini/nwmatcher/) and ."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:29
msgid "🥼 Reliably great performance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:31
msgid "Why?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:33
msgid ""
"Most CSS engines written in JavaScript execute selectors left-to-right. "
"That means thet execute every component of the selector in order, from "
"left to right. As an example: For the selector `a b`, these engines will "
"first query for `a` elements, then search these for `b` elements. (That's"
" the approach of eg. [`Sizzle`](https://github.com/jquery/sizzle), "
"[`Qwery`](https://github.com/ded/qwery) and "
"[`NWMatcher`](https://github.com/dperini/nwmatcher/).)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:41
msgid ""
"While this works, it has some downsides: Children of `a`s will be checked"
" multiple times; first, to check if they are also `a`s, then, for every "
"superior `a` once, if they are `b`s. Using [Big O "
"notation](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_O_notation), that would be "
"`O(n^(k+1))`, where `k` is the number of descendant selectors (that's the"
" space in the example above)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:48
msgid ""
"The far more efficient approach is to first look for `b` elements, then "
"check if they have superior `a` elements: Using big O notation again, "
"that would be `O(n)`. That's called right-to-left execution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:52
msgid "And that's what css-select does – and why it's quite performant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:54
msgid "How does it work?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:56
msgid "By building a stack of functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:58
msgid "_Wait, what?_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:60
msgid ""
"Okay, so let's suppose we want to compile the selector `a b`, for right-"
"to-left execution. We start by _parsing_ the selector. This turns the "
"selector into an array of the building blocks. That's what the [`css-"
"what`](https://github.com/fb55/css-what) module is for, if you want to "
"have a look."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:66
msgid "Anyway, after parsing, we end up with an array like this one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:76
msgid ""
"(Actually, this array is wrapped in another array, but that's another "
"story, involving commas in selectors.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:79
msgid ""
"Now that we know the meaning of every part of the selector, we can "
"compile it. That is where things become interesting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:82
msgid ""
"The basic idea is to turn every part of the selector into a function, "
"which takes an element as its only argument. The function checks whether "
"a passed element matches its part of the selector: If it does, the "
"element is passed to the next function representing the next part of the "
"selector. That function does the same. If an element is accepted by all "
"parts of the selector, it _matches_ the selector and double rainbow ALL "
"THE WAY."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:89
msgid ""
"As said before, we want to do right-to-left execution with all the big O "
"improvements. That means elements are passed from the rightmost part of "
"the selector (`b` in our example) to the leftmost (~~which would be `c`~~"
" of course `a`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:94
msgid ""
"For traversals, such as the _descendant_ operating the space between `a` "
"and `b`, we walk up the DOM tree, starting from the element passed as "
"argument."
msgstr ""

