msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:99
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:105
msgid ""
"**Note:** css-select throws errors when invalid selectors are passed to "
"it. This is done to aid with writing css selectors, but can be unexpected"
" when processing arbitrary strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:109
msgid "`CSSselect.selectAll(query, elems, options)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:111
msgid "Queries `elems`, returns an array containing all matches."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:113
msgid "`query` can be either a CSS selector or a function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:114
msgid ""
"`elems` can be either an array of elements, or a single element. If it is"
" an element, its children will be queried."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:116
msgid "`options` is described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:118
msgid "Aliases: `default` export, `CSSselect.iterate(query, elems)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:120
msgid "`CSSselect.compile(query, options)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:122
msgid "Compiles the query, returns a function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:124
msgid "`CSSselect.is(elem, query, options)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:126
msgid ""
"Tests whether or not an element is matched by `query`. `query` can be "
"either a CSS selector or a function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:129
msgid "`CSSselect.selectOne(query, elems, options)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:131
msgid ""
"Arguments are the same as for `CSSselect.selectAll(query, elems)`. Only "
"returns the first match, or `null` if there was no match."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:134
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:136
msgid "All options are optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:138
msgid ""
"`xmlMode`: When enabled, tag names will be case-sensitive. Default: "
"`false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:139
msgid ""
"`rootFunc`: The last function in the stack, will be called with the last "
"element that's looked at."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:141
msgid ""
"`adapter`: The adapter to use when interacting with the backing DOM "
"structure. By default it uses the `domutils` module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:143
msgid ""
"`context`: The context of the current query. Used to limit the scope of "
"searches. Can be matched directly using the `:scope` pseudo-class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:145
msgid ""
"`relativeSelector`: By default, selectors are relative to the `context`, "
"which means that no parent elements of the context will be matched. (Eg. "
"`a b c` with context `b` will never give any results.) If "
"`relativeSelector` is set to `false`, selectors won't be "
"[absolutized](http://www.w3.org/TR/selectors4/#absolutizing) and "
"selectors can test for parent elements outside of the `context`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:151
msgid ""
"`cacheResults`: Allow css-select to cache results for some selectors, "
"sometimes greatly improving querying performance. Disable this if your "
"document can change in between queries with the same compiled selector. "
"Default: `true`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:155
msgid "`pseudos`: A map of pseudo-class names to functions or strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:157
msgid "Custom Adapters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:159
msgid ""
"A custom adapter must match the interface described "
"[here](https://github.com/fb55/css-"
"select/blob/1aa44bdd64aaf2ebdfd7f338e2e76bed36521957/src/types.ts#L6-L96)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/css-select_README.md:162
msgid ""
"You may want to have a look at "
"[`domutils`](https://github.com/fb55/domutils) to see the default "
"implementation, or at [`css-select-browser-"
"adapter`](https://github.com/nrkn/css-select-browser-"
"adapter/blob/master/index.js) for an implementation backed by the DOM."
msgstr ""

